Python Control Flow :
Title: Tuple Conversion to list

Concept:
Tuples are immutable — their elements cannot be modified once defined.
To modify or perform operations like append, remove, etc., we can convert a tuple into a list using the list() function.
This helps in situations where we need flexibility (mutable data).

Tech used :
Language : pyhton
Compiler : Visual Studio Code

Logic Flow:
list(tpl_1) takes each element of the tuple and stores it in a new list.
The data type of the result becomes <class 'list'>.
You can now modify this list freely (add, remove, or change elements).
